# No alert() or confirm()

**Never use `alert()` or `confirm()`.** Use in-app components instead.

## Pattern

### Feedback
Use `v-alert` on the parent page with `type="error"` or `type="success"`, `density="compact"`, `class="mb-4"`.

### Confirmations
Use `StandardDialog` with Cancel and primary action buttons. Never use raw `v-dialog`.

```vue
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<v-alert v-if="error" type="error" density="compact" class="mb-4">{{ error }}</v-alert>

<StandardDialog v-model="showConfirm" title="Delete screen?" max-width="400">
  <p>Are you sure?</p>
  <template #actions>
    <v-spacer />
    <v-btn variant="text" class="mr-2" @click="showConfirm = false">Cancel</v-btn>
    <v-btn color="error" variant="elevated" @click="doDelete">Delete</v-btn>
  </template>
</StandardDialog>

<!-- ❌ BAD -->
confirm('Are you sure?')
alert('Error!')
```
